## Highlights
Complete reduction of $\mathrm{{Cu^{\mathrm{{II}}}}}$ to highly dispersive $\mathrm{Cu^{\mathrm{I}}}$ was achieved on MIL-101.   
Both cobalt doping and keeping metal sites at the interior of MIL-101 facilitate the dispersion and reduction.   
CuCoM-DS adsorbents show superior performances in $\mathrm{C_{2}H_{4}/C_{2}H_{6}}$ separation to MIL-101, CuCoM-WI, CuCoM-SG and CuM-DS.
